4. ROYALTY STRUCTURE & PAYMENT TERMS
================================================================================

4.1 ROYALTY RATE FOR COMMERCIAL USE

All Licensees engaged in Commercial Use must pay royalties as follows:

    TIERED ROYALTY STRUCTURE:
    
    Tier 1: 5% of Gross Revenue
    - Applies to the first $100,000 in annual Gross Revenue generated from
      products/services using the Software
    
    Tier 2: 7% of Gross Revenue
    - Applies to Gross Revenue between $100,001 and $1,000,000 annually
    
    Tier 3: 10% of Gross Revenue
    - Applies to all Gross Revenue exceeding $1,000,000 annually

4.2 FLAT ANNUAL LICENSE FEE

In addition to royalty payments, Licensee must pay a minimum annual flat fee
based on the tiered structure below. Whichever amount is greater (the tiered 
percentage of revenue OR the corresponding flat annual fee) must be paid annually:

    Tier 1 Flat Fee: $50,000/year minimum
    - Applies when annual Gross Revenue is $0 - $100,000
    
    Tier 2 Flat Fee: $250,000/year minimum
    - Applies when annual Gross Revenue is $100,001 - $1,000,000
    
    Tier 3 Flat Fee: $500,000/year minimum
    - Applies when annual Gross Revenue is $1,000,001 - $1,500,000
    
    Tier 4 Flat Fee: $500,000 PLUS 50% of all revenue exceeding $1,500,000
    - Applies when annual Gross Revenue exceeds $1,500,000
    - Example: If revenue is $2,000,000, the fee is $500,000 + (50% of $500,000) = $750,000

    The flat annual fee is separate from and in addition to percentage-based
    royalties. Licensee pays whichever amount is greater: the percentage-based
    royalty calculation OR the flat fee.

4.3 RETROACTIVE PAYMENT OBLIGATION

If Licensee has already used the Software commercially WITHOUT a license:

    a) Licensee must immediately pay an UPFRONT DISCOVERY FEE of $50,000
    
    b) Licensee must immediately pay 50% of all Gross Revenue generated from 
       commercial use since first deployment (or best estimate)
    
    c) Interest accrues at 25% annually on all unpaid amounts from the date
       of first commercial use
    
    d) Licensee must provide a full accounting of all past revenue generated
       from the Software, certified by an independent accountant
    
    e) Failure to disclose retroactive use will result in FIVE TIMES (5x) 
       the penalty on all owed royalties, plus legal fees and court costs

    RETROACTIVE PAYMENT EXAMPLE:
    - If Licensee made $100,000 in revenue using the Software:
      * $50,000 upfront discovery fee (non-negotiable)
      * $50,000 (50% of $100,000 revenue)
      * 25% annual interest on the $50,000 from date of first use
      * Total owed = $100,000+ (depending on how long they used it)

4.4 PAYMENT SCHEDULE

    a) Royalties are calculated and due bimonthly (every 60 days)
    b) Licensee must submit a Royalty Report along with each payment
    c) Reports must include:
       - Total Gross Revenue for the 60-day period
       - Breakdown of revenue sources using the Software
       - Calculation of royalties owed
       - Any refunds or credits claimed
    d) Payments are due within 30 days of the 60-day reporting period end
    e) Late payments accrue interest at 2% per month (24% annually)

4.5 MINIMUM COMMITMENT

Licensee commits to pay the applicable flat annual fee every year the 
Commercial License is in effect, regardless of revenue generated. Flat fees
are non-refundable.

