4.6.2 MODIFICATIONS REQUIRE DOCUMENTED CONSENT

Any modification to the pricing structure, royalty rates, flat fees, or payment
terms outlined in this license MUST:

    a) Be submitted to the Original Creator in writing
    b) Be negotiated and agreed upon by both parties
    c) Be documented in a separate Custom License Agreement
    d) Be signed and dated by an authorized representative of the Original Creator
       (2c9jj9rmgj-code or designated legal representative)
    e) Include explicit language identifying what terms are being modified
    f) Become effective only upon the date both parties have executed the agreement

4.6.3 DEFAULT TERMS APPLY UNTIL CUSTOM AGREEMENT IS SIGNED

Until a Custom License Agreement is executed and signed by the Original Creator,
all default terms outlined in Section 4 (Sections 4.1 through 4.5) apply in
their entirety with NO exceptions, modifications, or alternatives.

4.6.4 CUSTOM AGREEMENT TAKES PRECEDENCE

If a Custom License Agreement has been negotiated and signed between the Original
Creator and Licensee, that Custom License Agreement supersedes the default terms
outlined in Section 4, but ONLY for the specific terms explicitly modified in
the Custom License Agreement. All other terms from this base license remain in
full force and effect.

4.6.5 NO UNILATERAL MODIFICATION

Licensee may not:
    a) Unilaterally change, reduce, or modify any pricing or payment terms
    b) Claim an agreement exists without signed documentation from the Original Creator
    c) Rely on verbal agreements, emails without formal signatures, or informal 
       communications as a basis for modifying these terms
    d) Treat any negotiation or discussion as a binding modification

4.6.6 DISPUTES OVER PRICING

If Licensee disputes the pricing structure or payment obligations, Licensee must:
    a) Contact the Original Creator immediately at the contact information in Section 12
    b) Submit a formal written request for negotiation
    c) Await written response from the Original Creator
    d) Not cease payments of the default terms while negotiation is ongoing
    e) Understand that non-payment during negotiation may be treated as breach of
       this license

4.6.7 RENEWAL AND MODIFICATION

Any modifications to this agreement, including price changes, term extensions, or
adjustments to royalty rates, must be formalized in writing with proper signature
authority before the modification takes effect. Licensee will be provided written
notice of any pricing changes or modifications at least 60 days before they take effect,
except in cases where Licensee has breached the agreement.

